{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s59-p01",
      "text": "Have you ever imagined the life in space?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p02",
      "text": "The following will show you the astronauts' daily life.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p03",
      "text": "Eating in space",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p04",
      "text": "Some foods can be eaten in their natural forms, such as chocolate cakes and bananas.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p05",
      "text": "Other foods require adding water, such as cheese.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p06",
      "text": "Of course, an oven is provided at the space station to heat the food.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p07",
      "text": "But there are no fridges, so space food must be kept properly.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p08",
      "text": "Astronauts can never be careless with their food storage.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p09",
      "text": "Sleeping in space",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p10",
      "text": "Astronauts go to bed at a certain time, then get up and prepare for work again.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p11",
      "text": "They might set their alarm clocks to wake up at 6 a.m.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p12",
      "text": "When going to sleep, they have to attach themselves, so they don't float around or hit their bodies against something.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p13",
      "text": "They usually use sleeping bags located in small crew cabins.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p14",
      "text": "Each crew cabin is like a tiny apartment just big enough for one person.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p15",
      "text": "Exercise is an important part of every astronaut's daily life to prevent muscle loss.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p16",
      "text": "Usually, astronauts exercise two hours every day.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p17",
      "text": "They might use a special gym with exercise machines.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p18",
      "text": "Lifting 200 pounds on Earth may be a lot of work, but it would be much easier in space.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p19-01",
      "text": "That means the things for exercise need to be specially designed,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p19-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p19-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p19-02",
      "text": "so astronauts can receive the exercise needed to stay fit.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p19-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p19-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p20",
      "text": "Living in space is not just all work and no play.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p21",
      "text": "Astronauts have fun too.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p22",
      "text": "They might take photos of Earth or write in their diaries.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p22.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p22.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s59-p23",
      "text": "Fun plays an important role in the quality of their lives.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p23.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s59-p23.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
